https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/Cutsat/Types.lean#L161-L177"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">structure</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/Cutsat/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.Cutsat.CooperSplitPred\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">Arith</span>.<span class=\"name\">Cutsat</span>.<span class=\"name\">CooperSplitPred</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The predicate of type `Nat → Prop`, which serves as the conclusion of the\n`cooper_left`, `cooper_right`, `cooper_dvd_left`, and `cooper_dvd_right` theorems.\n\nThe specific predicate used is determined as follows:\n- `cooper_left_split` (if `left` is `true` and `c₃?` is `none`)\n- `cooper_right_split` (if `left` is `false` and `c₃?` is `none`)\n- `cooper_dvd_left_split` (if `left` is `true` and `c₃?` is `some`)\n- `cooper_dvd_right_split` (if `left` is `false` and `c₃?` is `some`)\n\nSee `CooperSplit`","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/Cutsat/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.Cutsat.CooperSplitPred","kind":"structure","line":161,"name":"Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.Cutsat.CooperSplitPred","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/Cutsat/Types.lean#L161-L177"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">abbrev</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/Cutsat/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.Cutsat.DvdCnstr.depth?\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">Arith</span>.<span class=\"name\">Cutsat</span