sic.html#Int\">Int</a> → <a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/Cutsat/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.Cutsat.OrHullAlt\">Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.Cutsat.OrHullAlt</a></span></span></span></span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/Cutsat/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.Cutsat.OrHullAlt.mk","kind":"ctor","line":75,"name":"Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.Cutsat.OrHullAlt.mk","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/Cutsat/Types.lean#L75-L89"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">structure</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/Cutsat/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.Cutsat.OrHullAlt\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">Arith</span>.<span class=\"name\">Cutsat</span>.<span class=\"name\">OrHullAlt</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"How the disjunct of an `.orHull` constraint implies it. The disjunct is a conjunction, and its\nconjunct at `path` (`false` for `And.left`, `true` for `And.right`) is `a = b` (`eq` and `eqNeg`)\nor `a ≤ b` (`le`), where `lhs` and `rhs` represent `a` and `b` (after the cast to `Int` given by\n`toIntThm?` if they are natural numbers). The polynomial `p := (lhs.sub rhs).norm` satisfies\n`p ≤ 0` (`le`), `p = 0` (`eq`), or `-p = 0` (`eqNeg`), and is the constraint plus `k ≥ 0`.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/Cutsat/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.Cutsat.OrHullAlt","kind":"structure","line":75,"name":"Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.Cutsat.OrHullAlt","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/Cutsat/Types.lean#L75-L89"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_heade